From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DREAM <dream@invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:35:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HE-AAC v1/v2 with a 12 kHz core (24 kHz output)

SBR/PS were silently replaced by AAC-LC for inputs below 32 kHz (ixheaace_api.c), and a
missing break in ixheaace_is_sbr_setting_available() made mono need >= 32 kHz too. Inputs
from 16 kHz up are now accepted and the tuning table decides; combinations without a tuning
entry fail init instead of encoding AAC-LC. Adds stereo tuning rows for the 12 kHz core
(needed for stereo SBR and, via the availability check, for PS): start/stop band from the
12 kHz mono row at the per-channel bitrate (16-24 kbit/s: {7,11}; >= 24 kbit/s: {11,12}),
noise and stereo parameters as in the 16 kHz-core stereo rows.
---
 encoder/ixheaace_api.c      |  6 +++++-
 encoder/ixheaace_sbr_main.c | 10 ++++++----
 encoder/ixheaace_sbr_rom.c  | 10 +++++++++-
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/encoder/ixheaace_api.c b/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
index 6d5c47e..bca0a88 100644
--- a/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
+++ b/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
@@ -901,7 +901,11 @@ static IA_ERRORCODE ixheaace_set_config_params(ixheaace_api_struct *pstr_api_str
         (AOT_AAC_ELD == pstr_input_config->aot)) {
       pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].aac_classic = 0;
     }
-    if (pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].sample_rate < 32000) {
+    /* HE-AAC (AOT 5/29) needs a dual-rate SBR tuning entry for core rate = input rate / 2.
+       Entries exist from an 8 kHz core up, e.g. DRM's 24 kHz output with a 12 kHz core, so only
+       inputs below 16 kHz fall back to AAC-LC here; unsupported combinations are rejected by
+       ixheaace_is_sbr_setting_available() during init instead of silently encoding AAC-LC. */
+    if (pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].sample_rate < 16000) {
       if (pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].aac_classic == 0) {
         pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].aac_classic = 1;
       }
diff --git a/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_main.c b/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_main.c
index c2c95ca..2b5d4bb 100644
--- a/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_main.c
+++ b/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_main.c
@@ -395,13 +395,15 @@ ixheaace_is_sbr_setting_available(UWORD32 bitrate, UWORD32 num_output_channels,
 
   switch (num_output_channels) {
     case MONO:
-      if (sample_rate_input < 16000 || sample_rate_input > 48000) {
-        return 0;
-      }
     case STEREO:
-      if (sample_rate_input < 32000 || sample_rate_input > 48000) {
+      /* availability below 32 kHz is decided by the tuning table (stereo rows exist for 12 and
+         16 kHz cores); the missing break made mono require >= 32 kHz as well */
+      if (sample_rate_input < 16000 || sample_rate_input > 48000) {
         return 0;
       }
+      break;
+    default:
+      break;
   }
 
   *ptr_core_sr = sample_rate_input / 2;
diff --git a/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_rom.c b/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_rom.c
index 90e94c5..00c7b82 100644
--- a/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_rom.c
+++ b/encoder/ixheaace_sbr_rom.c
@@ -637,7 +637,15 @@ const ixheaace_str_qmf_tabs ixheaace_qmf_tab = {
        {10000, 12000, {7, 11}, 3, {1, 0, 6}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_MONO},
        {12000, 72001, {11, 12}, 3, {1, 0, 6}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_MONO},
        {0}},
-      {{0}}},
+      /* 12 kHz core, stereo (24 kHz output, e.g. DRM). Derived: the per-channel bitrate B/2
+         selects the start/stop band of the 12 kHz mono rows above (the 8-10 kbit/s mono row
+         {4, 6} yields no decodable HF, so 16-20 kbit/s also uses {7, 11}); noise and stereo
+         parameters follow the 16 kHz-core stereo rows (1 noise band and -3 dB max level, 2 noise
+         bands from 28 kbit/s, SWITCH_LRC). */
+      {{16000, 24000, {7, 11}, 3, {1, 0, -3}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_SWITCH_LRC},
+       {24000, 28000, {11, 12}, 3, {1, 0, -3}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_SWITCH_LRC},
+       {28000, 144001, {11, 12}, 3, {2, 0, -3}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_SWITCH_LRC},
+       {0}}},
 
      {{{8000, 10000, {1, 0}, 3, {1, 0, 6}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_MONO},
        {10000, 12000, {2, 6}, 3, {1, 0, 6}, IXHEAACE_SBR_MODE_MONO},
